{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"agent_message","text":"Instrumentation localized the crash to the first insert into `stbds_shmode_func(..., 4)`. C stores mode `4` in the table, falls through the storage switch’s binary `memcpy`, then later interprets those bytes as a string pointer; that path has no defined result. I’m testing high out-of-range API modes through `stbds_hmput_key(NULL, ..., mode)` instead, where C normalizes any `mode >= 1` to default string storage, and retaining `shmode_func` coverage for its named modes."}}
